# Tier-0 hygiene: CODEOWNERS for KWatch
#
# Each line is a file pattern followed by one or more owners.
# Order matters: the last matching pattern takes precedence.
# See https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Default owner for everything in the repo.
#
# KWatch is a single-maintainer project at the moment, so the default
# owner is the GitHub handle of the project owner. As the Phenotype
# org grows and additional maintainers get triage rights, layer
# `@Phenotype-org/<team>` patterns on top of this default rather than
# replacing it (the last matching pattern wins, so team entries should
# come BELOW the catch-all `*` line).
* @kooshapari

# Security-critical paths — require review from the security owner.
# Until a dedicated security team exists, the owner is the same handle.
SECURITY.md        @kooshapari
.gitleaks.toml     @kooshapari
.github/workflows/audit.yml     @kooshapari
.github/workflows/scorecard.yml @kooshapari

# CI/CD workflows — require review from the platform owner.
# Until a dedicated platform team exists, the owner is the same handle.
.github/workflows/ @kooshapari

# Go source code
*.go               @kooshapari

# Documentation
*.md               @kooshapari
